---
import globalStyles from "../styles/global.css?raw";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Publication archive by Fernando Miramontes Forattini across historical sociology, governance, inequality, and sociotechnical systems."
    />
    <title>Publications | Fernando Miramontes Forattini</title>
    <style is:global set:html={globalStyles}></style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header" aria-label="Site header">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Fernando Miramontes Forattini homepage">
        <span class="brand-mark">Fernando Miramontes Forattini</span>
        <span class="brand-sub">Historical Sociology · Governance · Technology</span>
      </a>

      <nav class="site-nav" id="site-nav" data-site-nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="/#agenda">Agenda</a>
        <a href="/research/">Research</a>
        <a href="/publications/">Publications</a>
        <a href="/#teaching">Teaching</a>
        <a href="/#projects">Applied Work</a>
        <a href="/cv/fernando-miramontes-forattini-cv.docx" download>CV</a>
        <a href="/#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>

      <button class="menu-button" type="button" data-menu-button aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-nav">
        <span class="menu-lines" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="sr-only">Open menu</span>
      </button>
    </header>

    <main class="subpage-main">
      <section class="subpage-hero">
        <p class="section-kicker">Publications</p>
        <h1 class="section-title">Publications archive.</h1>
        <p class="section-copy">
          A working archive of selected and forthcoming publications. This page can later expand
          with filters, DOI links, BibTeX, downloadable PDFs, and full citation metadata.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="publication-section" id="governance" aria-labelledby="governance-title">
        <p class="section-kicker">Cluster 01</p>
        <h2 id="governance-title">Governance, corruption, and institutional power</h2>
        <div class="work-grid">
          <article class="work-card featured">
            <div>
              <p class="meta">Cambridge University Press · 2026</p>
              <h3>The contingency of mobilization: The social contexts of Operation Lava Jato in Brazil.</h3>
            </div>
            <p>In <em>A comparative historical sociology of corruption</em>.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">American Behavioral Scientist · 2026</p>
            <h3>Beyond “best practices”: A historical-sociological critique of privatization, decentralization, and anti-corruption reforms in 1990s Brazil.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">MIT Press · 2026</p>
            <h3>The rise and evolution of anti-corruption impulses in the United States and Brazil.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">Palgrave Macmillan · 2026</p>
            <h3>Fighting sexual corruption in public services: Lessons from women’s experiences in Brazil.</h3>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="publication-section" id="classification" aria-labelledby="classification-title">
        <p class="section-kicker">Cluster 02</p>
        <h2 id="classification-title">Inequality, classification, and recognition</h2>
        <div class="work-grid">
          <article class="work-card featured">
            <p class="meta">Oxford University Press · 2026</p>
            <h3>The weight of the “pardo” category: Official statistics and the deracialization of Indigenous peoples.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">Cronos · 2023</p>
            <h3>Produção e reprodução das desigualdades sociais relacionadas à COVID-19 expressas nas redes sociais.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">European Review of Latin American and Caribbean Studies · 2020</p>
            <h3>Piripkura: The plight of Indigenous people, environment, and Brazilian identity.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">Culture, identity, and political imagination</p>
            <h3>Superman e a virada conservadora de Reagan.</h3>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="publication-section" id="technology" aria-labelledby="technology-title">
        <p class="section-kicker">Cluster 03</p>
        <h2 id="technology-title">Technology, AI, and sociotechnical governance</h2>
        <div class="work-grid">
          <article class="work-card featured">
            <p class="meta">European Journal of Information Systems · under review</p>
            <h3>When Promethean leaps meet institutional power: Designing digital public services through a care-ethical lens.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">Information Systems Management · 2026</p>
            <h3>Prometheus ambition, Zeusian order: Why leaps in information systems require structurally aware ethical frameworks.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">ACM SIGMIS Database · 2026</p>
            <h3>From design to policy: Embedding care ethics and STEM institutional insights in gender-focused technology.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">ACM SIGMIS Database · 2025</p>
            <h3>Breaking boundaries: Advancing gender and technology research to combat sextortion.</h3>
          </article>
          <article class="work-card">
            <p class="meta">HICSS · 2026</p>
            <h3>AI agents in gender-sensitive public service encounters.</h3>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <span>© 2026 Fernando Miramontes Forattini</span>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
    </footer>

    <script>
      import "../scripts/scroll-story.js";
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
